113@@@@1@@"I am sure that I shall say nothing of the kind."@@@@1@11@sid=11013@@
114@@@@1@@"You see, my dear Watson,"--he propped his test-tube in the rack, and began to lecture with the air of a professor addressing his class--"it is not really difficult to construct a series of inferences, each dependent upon its predecessor and each simple in itself.@@@@1@44@sid=11014@@
115@@@@1@@If, after doing so, one simply knocks out all the central inferences and presents one's audience with the starting-point and the conclusion, one may produce a startling, though possibly a meretricious, effect.@@@@1@32@sid=11015@@
116@@@@1@@Now, it was not really difficult, by an inspection of the groove between your left forefinger and thumb, to feel sure that you did NOT propose to invest your small capital in the gold fields."@@@@1@35@sid=11016@@
117@@@@1@@"I see no connection."@@@@1@4@sid=11017@@
118@@@@1@@"Very likely not; but I can quickly show you a close connection.@@@@1@12@sid=11018@@
119@@@@1@@Here are the missing links of the very simple chain: 1. You had chalk between your left finger and thumb when you returned from the club last night.@@@@1@28@sid=11019@@
120@@@@1@@2. You put chalk there when you play billiards, to steady the cue.@@@@1@13@sid=11020@@
121@@@@1@@3. You never play billiards except with Thurston.@@@@1@8@sid=11021@@
122@@@@1@@4. You told me, four weeks ago, that Thurston had an option on some South African property which would expire in a month, and which he desired you to share with him.@@@@1@32@sid=11022@@
123@@@@1@@5. Your check book is locked in my drawer, and you have not asked for the key.@@@@1@17@sid=11023@@
124@@@@1@@6. You do not propose to invest your money in this manner."@@@@1@12@sid=11024@@
125@@@@1@@"How absurdly simple!" I cried.@@@@1@5@sid=11025@@
126@@@@1@@"Quite so!" said he, a little nettled.@@@@1@7@sid=11026@@
