189@@@@1@@"Well, now I come to the queer part of my story.@@@@1@11@sid=11091@@
190@@@@1@@About a week ago--it was the Tuesday of last week--I found on one of the window-sills a number of absurd little dancing figures like these upon the paper.@@@@1@28@sid=11092@@
191@@@@1@@They were scrawled with chalk.@@@@1@5@sid=11093@@
192@@@@1@@I thought that it was the stable-boy who had drawn them, but the lad swore he knew nothing about it.@@@@1@20@sid=11094@@
193@@@@1@@Anyhow, they had come there during the night.@@@@1@8@sid=11095@@
194@@@@1@@I had them washed out, and I only mentioned the matter to my wife afterwards.@@@@1@15@sid=11096@@
195@@@@1@@To my surprise, she took it very seriously, and begged me if any more came to let her see them.@@@@1@20@sid=11097@@
196@@@@1@@None did come for a week, and then yesterday morning I found this paper lying on the sundial in the garden.@@@@1@21@sid=11098@@
197@@@@1@@I showed it to Elsie, and down she dropped in a dead faint.@@@@1@13@sid=11099@@
198@@@@1@@Since then she has looked like a woman in a dream, half dazed, and with terror always lurking in her eyes.@@@@1@21@sid=11100@@
199@@@@1@@It was then that I wrote and sent the paper to you, Mr. Holmes.@@@@1@14@sid=11101@@
200@@@@1@@It was not a thing that I could take to the police, for they would have laughed at me, but you will tell me what to do.@@@@1@27@sid=11102@@
201@@@@1@@I am not a rich man, but if there is any danger threatening my little woman, I would spend my last copper to shield her."@@@@1@25@sid=11103@@
202@@@@1@@He was a fine creature, this man of the old English soil--simple, straight, and gentle, with his great, earnest blue eyes and broad, comely face.@@@@1@25@sid=11104@@
203@@@@1@@His love for his wife and his trust in her shone in his features.@@@@1@14@sid=11105@@
204@@@@1@@Holmes had listened to his story with the utmost attention, and now he sat for some time in silent thought.@@@@1@20@sid=11106@@
205@@@@1@@"Don't you think, Mr.  Cubitt," said he, at last, "that your best plan would be to make a direct appeal to your wife, and to ask her to share her secret with you?"@@@@1@33@sid=11107@@
206@@@@1@@Hilton Cubitt shook his massive head.@@@@1@6@sid=11108@@
207@@@@1@@"A promise is a promise, Mr. Holmes.@@@@1@7@sid=11109@@
208@@@@1@@If Elsie wished to tell me she would.@@@@1@8@sid=11110@@
209@@@@1@@If not, it is not for me to force her confidence.@@@@1@11@sid=11111@@
210@@@@1@@But I am justified in taking my own line--and I will."@@@@1@11@sid=11112@@
