212@@@@1@@In the first place, have you heard of any strangers being seen in your neighbourhood?"@@@@1@15@sid=11114@@
213@@@@1@@"No."@@@@1@1@sid=11115@@
214@@@@1@@"I presume that it is a very quiet place.@@@@1@9@sid=11116@@
215@@@@1@@Any fresh face would cause comment?"@@@@1@6@sid=11117@@
216@@@@1@@"In the immediate neighbourhood, yes.@@@@1@5@sid=11118@@
217@@@@1@@But we have several small watering-places not very far away.@@@@1@10@sid=11119@@
218@@@@1@@And the farmers take in lodgers."@@@@1@6@sid=11120@@
219@@@@1@@"These hieroglyphics have evidently a meaning.@@@@1@6@sid=11121@@
220@@@@1@@If it is a purely arbitrary one, it may be impossible for us to solve it.@@@@1@16@sid=11122@@
221@@@@1@@If, on the other hand, it is systematic, I have no doubt that we shall get to the bottom of it.@@@@1@21@sid=11123@@
222@@@@1@@But this particular sample is so short that I can do nothing, and the facts which you have brought me are so indefinite that we have no basis for an investigation.@@@@1@31@sid=11124@@
223@@@@1@@I would suggest that you return to Norfolk, that you keep a keen lookout, and that you take an exact copy of any fresh dancing men which may appear.@@@@1@29@sid=11125@@
