226@@@@1@@When you have collected some fresh evidence, come to me again.@@@@1@11@sid=11128@@
227@@@@1@@That is the best advice which I can give you, Mr. Hilton Cubitt.@@@@1@13@sid=11129@@
228@@@@1@@If there are any pressing fresh developments, I shall be always ready to run down and see you in your Norfolk home."@@@@1@22@sid=11130@@
229@@@@1@@The interview left Sherlock Holmes very thoughtful, and several times in the next few days I saw him take his slip of paper from his notebook and look long and earnestly at the curious figures inscribed upon it.@@@@1@38@sid=11131@@
230@@@@1@@He made no allusion to the affair, however, until one afternoon a fortnight or so later.@@@@1@16@sid=11132@@
231@@@@1@@I was going out when he called me back.@@@@1@9@sid=11133@@
232@@@@1@@"You had better stay here, Watson."@@@@1@6@sid=11134@@
233@@@@1@@"Why?"@@@@1@1@sid=11135@@
234@@@@1@@"Because I had a wire from Hilton Cubitt this morning.@@@@1@10@sid=11136@@
235@@@@1@@You remember Hilton Cubitt, of the dancing men?@@@@1@8@sid=11137@@
236@@@@1@@He was to reach Liverpool Street at one-twenty.@@@@1@8@sid=11138@@
237@@@@1@@He may be here at any moment.@@@@1@7@sid=11139@@
238@@@@1@@I gather from his wire that there have been some new incidents of importance."@@@@1@14@sid=11140@@
239@@@@1@@We had not long to wait, for our Norfolk squire came straight from the station as fast as a hansom could bring him.@@@@1@23@sid=11141@@
240@@@@1@@He was looking worried and depressed, with tired eyes and a lined forehead.@@@@1@13@sid=11142@@
241@@@@1@@"It's getting on my nerves, this business, Mr. Holmes," said he, as he sank, like a wearied man, into an armchair.@@@@1@21@sid=11143@@
242@@@@1@@"It's bad enough to feel that you are surrounded by unseen, unknown folk, who have some kind of design upon you, but when, in addition to that, you know that it is just killing your wife by inches, then it becomes as much as flesh and blood can endure.@@@@1@49@sid=11144@@
243@@@@1@@She's wearing away under it--just wearing away before my eyes."@@@@1@10@sid=11145@@
244@@@@1@@"Has she said anything yet?"@@@@1@5@sid=11146@@
245@@@@1@@"No, Mr. Holmes, she has not.@@@@1@6@sid=11147@@
246@@@@1@@And yet there have been times when the poor girl has wanted to speak, and yet could not quite bring herself to take the plunge.@@@@1@25@sid=11148@@
247@@@@1@@I have tried to help her, but I daresay I did it clumsily, and scared her from it.@@@@1@18@sid=11149@@
248@@@@1@@She has spoken about my old family, and our reputation in the county, and our pride in our unsullied honour, and I always felt it was leading to the point, but somehow it turned off before we got there."@@@@1@39@sid=11150@@
249@@@@1@@"But you have found out something for yourself?"@@@@1@8@sid=11151@@
250@@@@1@@"A good deal, Mr. Holmes.@@@@1@5@sid=11152@@
