275@@@@1@@She answered that it was some senseless practical joke, and that I should not take any notice of it.@@@@1@19@sid=11178@@
276@@@@1@@"'If it really annoys you, Hilton, we might go and travel, you and I, and so avoid this nuisance.'@@@@1@19@sid=11179@@
277@@@@1@@"'What, be driven out of our own house by a practical joker?' said I.@@@@1@14@sid=11180@@
278@@@@1@@"'Well, come to bed,' said she, 'and we can discuss it in the morning.'@@@@1@14@sid=11182@@
279@@@@1@@"Suddenly, as she spoke, I saw her white face grow whiter yet in the moonlight, and her hand tightened upon my shoulder.@@@@1@22@sid=11183@@
280@@@@1@@Something was moving in the shadow of the tool-house.@@@@1@9@sid=11184@@
281@@@@1@@I saw a dark, creeping figure which crawled round the corner and squatted in front of the door.@@@@1@18@sid=11185@@
